**Code** — `296fcf8` `rea-rs: objc class-name strings` (README.md + `crates/rea-core/src/macho_meta.rs` only):
- `MachoFacts::objc_strings: Vec<String>` and `MachoArch::objc_strings` (each fat slice carries its own list; empty slice → empty list).
- `objc_strings(mo)`: walks every section whose name contains `objc` (case-insensitive), collects NUL-terminated printable C strings in file order, capped at 128 with a `... N more` marker. A pointer-only section (`__objc_classlist`) contributes nothing; no `class_ro_t`/method list/protocol walking; no Swift demangling; a run with no terminating NUL stays unread. No section → empty list, parse unaffected.

**Verification** — `cargo build --offline` clean; `cargo test --workspace --offline` all green (rea-core 230, rea-mcp 10, rea-cli 4). Three new fixture tests: named-section strings (incl. slice parity), pointer/non-objc/unterminated/empty sections, and the 128-cap with `... 12 more`. Live smoke: a synthetic Mach-O with `__objc_classname` (strings) + `__objc_classlist` (pointers) returns the three strings on `facts` and the slice; `/bin/ls` returns an empty `objc_strings` without failing.

**Docs** — `98857d2` `rea-rs: docs retire the objc strings gap`: README `rea_macho` line names the new field; review.html `#now` updated to `296fcf8`, banner count 227→230, new Done-table row, and the enhanced-native gaps cell now names the ObjC strings while keeping Swift, value/UI trace, and the unwalked structures honest.

